# Patterns to ignore when building Helm packages.
#
# NOTE: a pattern must sit on a line of its OWN. "#" only starts a comment at the START of a
# line — a trailing comment becomes part of the pattern, which then matches nothing and the
# path is silently packaged. That is exactly what happened to the five entries below: each
# carried a trailing comment, so docs/, setup-local-ldap-testing/, scripts/, docker/ and
# argocd-application.yaml were all shipped inside the chart tarball, including
# setup-local-ldap-testing/ca-key.pem — a private key.
#
# Verify after editing this file:
#   helm package . && tar -tzf group-sync-operator-helm-*.tgz

# Standard VCS / editor / OS cruft
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.github-no-deploy/
*.tmproj
*.swp
*.bak
*.orig
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Repo assets that are NOT part of the deployable chart

# design docs
docs/

# local test-LDAP harness — also carries ca-key.pem, which must never ship
setup-local-ldap-testing/

# helper scripts
# scripts/ is NOT ignored on purpose. templates/tests/test-scripts-configmap.yaml loads the test
# scripts with .Files.Get, which returns EMPTY for an ignored path — the scripts shipped as 0 bytes
# and every test passed without executing anything.

# image build context
docker/

# ArgoCD wrapper, applied separately
argocd-application.yaml

CONTRIBUTING.md
rendered-templates.yaml
.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc
